/// The compile-time reflection descriptors.
///
/// `fields_of`, `enum_values_of`, and `variants_of` already produce values of
/// these types; this package gives them their written names.
///
/// They remain compile-time-only: naming a descriptor type does not make a
/// descriptor storable at run time.
// design.md "Compile-time reflection". The compiler contributes all three, so
// `meta.Field` is the identity M4b created rather than a second nominal type.
@(public)
package meta;

// The compiler contributes all three (`src/stdlib.odin`), and checks each
// declaration below against its public fields (design.md "`@(intrinsic)`").

/// A record field, as `fields_of` produces it: its name, its declared type,
/// and its declaration index.
@(intrinsic)
Field :: struct { name: string_view, type: type, index: int }

/// An enum member, as `enum_values_of` produces it: its name, its value in the
/// enum's backing type, and its declaration index.
@(intrinsic)
Enum_Value :: struct { name: string_view, value: int, index: int }

/// A union variant, as `variants_of` produces it: its label, its payload type
/// (`Unit` when it has none), and its declaration index.
@(intrinsic)
Variant :: struct { name: string_view, type: type, index: int }
